<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ slug }} — hosted by cervo</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
      max-width: 40rem;
      margin: 4rem auto;
      padding: 0 1.5rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: #2a2a2a;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
    code {
      background: #f0f0ee;
      padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      font-size: 0.9em;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    footer { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #777; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>You made it! 🎉</h1>
  <p>
    This site was successfully deployed using cervo on {{ deployed_at }},
    and is served at <a href="{{ url }}">{{ url }}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>About cervo</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/ericovis/cervo">Cervo</a> is a demo app for
    managing static website hosting on a shared VPS, created by
    Eric Magalhães a.k.a. <a href="https://ericovis.com">ericovis</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Updating this site</h2>
  <p>
    Everything here is managed by chatting with an AI — there is no
    dashboard and no server to log into. Point your AI tool of choice at
    cervo's MCP server:
  </p>
  <p><code>{{ mcp_url }}</code></p>
  <p>Then just ask. Try prompts like:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>“Authenticate with cervo”</li>
    <li>“List my websites”</li>
    <li>“Create a website called my-cool-site”</li>
  </ul>

  <footer>Hosted by <a href="https://github.com/ericovis/cervo">cervo</a>.</footer>
</body>
</html>
